  "shadow": {
    "1": {
      "$value": "0 1px 1.5px oklch(30% 0.04 260 / 0.06), 0 2px 6px -2px oklch(30% 0.04 260 / 0.06)"
    },
    "2": {
      "$value": "0 1px 2px oklch(28% 0.04 260 / 0.06), 0 3px 8px -3px oklch(28% 0.05 260 / 0.08), 0 12px 28px -12px oklch(24% 0.05 260 / 0.16)"
    },
    "3": {
      "$value": "0 2px 4px oklch(24% 0.05 260 / 0.06), 0 12px 28px -12px oklch(22% 0.06 260 / 0.16), 0 48px 96px -32px oklch(20% 0.06 260 / 0.30)"
    },
    "$description": "Depth is a ladder: room → sheet (3) → card (2) → the row or disc inside it (1). Every shadow is two-part — a contact shadow that says what the object touches, plus a wide ambient one that says how far it floats. One-part shadows read as stickers. The hue is the room's, not the ink's: a shadow is the room going dark, so it darkens in the room's own family (260). Still no inset shadows anywhere except the 1px light-catch on glass.",
    "$type": "shadow",
    "catch": {
      "$value": "inset 0 1px 0 {color.material.glass-line}",
      "$description": "The 1px light-catch on the top edge of glass, and on the window's top edge. Lighting, not an emboss: it is on nothing you press. Stated once and referenced by `rim-glass`, so the light that catches a rim is the same light that catches the sheet."
    },
    "rim-glass": {
      "$value": "{shadow.catch}, inset 0 -1px 0 {color.material.glass-bounce}, inset 0 0 0 1px {color.material.glass-rim}, inset 0 0 16px {color.material.glass-glow}, 0 0 0 1px {color.material.glass-veil}",
      "$description": "The boundary of the glass, lit all the way round: top catch, far edge, rim, inner glow, and the dark hairline outside the rim so the lit edge has a dark side. The only inset-shadow recipe in the system apart from `catch` itself, and it exists because on a near-white sheet the edge *is* the material."
    },
    "pop": {
      "$value": "0 4px 8px oklch(22% 0.05 260 / 0.08), 0 24px 56px -16px oklch(20% 0.06 260 / 0.22), 0 64px 128px -32px oklch(20% 0.06 260 / 0.34)"
    },
    "ink": {
      "$value": "0 1px 2px oklch(15% 0.02 260 / 0.20), 0 8px 20px -8px oklch(15% 0.02 260 / 0.30)"
    },
    "$dark": {
      "1": {
        "$value": "0 1px 1.5px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.35), 0 2px 6px -2px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.30)"
      },
      "2": {
        "$value": "0 1px 2px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.40), 0 3px 8px -3px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.35), 0 12px 28px -12px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.45)"
      },
      "3": {
        "$value": "0 2px 4px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.40), 0 12px 28px -12px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.50), 0 48px 96px -32px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.60)"
      },
      "pop": {
